corpus/fixtures/r96-crossing-response/README.md:9:The inherited paired-clock entries remain distinct tick-9 events: Aru's north lantern at Quiet Rise and Evin's south bell at Salt Court. The inherited tick-10 meeting at the Chalk Stair remains ordered after and explicitly dependent on both named tick-9 entries. The inherited tick-11 event is ordered after and depends on the tick-10 decision (`paired-crossing-decision`), and it records only Aru's report that he waited through the agreed bell and that Evin did not come. The new tick-12 event is ordered after and depends on that tick-11 report (`aftermath-missing-evin`), and it records only Evin's second account of the same occasion: that he was at Salt Court through the same agreed bell. It adds one second first-person account; it does not change earlier locations, resolve or create a contradiction, or convert either account into a verdict.
